        "original_id": "57625a3e-fa38-51b2-995a-4d4c4d0303c9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gemma Rovira Ortega, John Boyne, Patrick Rothfuss\n- Works: Harry Potter, The Boy in the Striped Pyjamas, The Kingkiller Chronicle\n- Places: Barcelona, Spain, UK, Ireland, Australia\n- Topics: Translation, Bestseller lists\n\nFacts:\n- Gemma Rovira Ortega was born in 1974 and is an English-Spanish translator from Barcelona.\n- Gemma Rovira Ortega is known for translating Harry Potter into Spanish.\n- Gemma Rovira Ortega is known for translating John Boyne’s The Boy in the Striped Pyjamas into Spanish.\n- Gemma Rovira Ortega is known for translating Patrick Rothfuss’s The Kingkiller Chronicle series into Spanish.\n- In 2007, The Boy in the Striped Pyjamas was the best-selling book of the year in Spain.\n- In 2008, The Boy in the Striped Pyjamas was again the best-selling book of the year in Spain.\n- The Boy in the Striped Pyjamas reached number one on the New York Times bestseller list and also reached number one in the UK, Ireland, and Australia.",
